--
dropped the body
--
__invoke_impl<_Partial<_Transform, ...>> and __invoke lose their bodies:
the call __f(__args...) of the _Partial closure object finds "no match for
symbol '_Partial'" (CBMC_CPP_SHOW_SUPPRESSED=1), as if the call named the
class's constructor rather than its member operator() template.  A
hand-written partial specialization called the same way works, so the cause
is in the remaining <ranges> context; not reduced further (cvise stopped at
its 2 h limit).  With libstdc++ 16 this is the drop of
cpp20_ranges_views_iota_transform_filter_drop (broken-libstdcxx16).
